{
  "version": "1.6.8.0",
  "name": "Tempester 1.6.8.0 — a second full backup no longer stops a voice",
  "kind": "release",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "summary": "Everything in 1.6.7.0; a second full backup (or Debug Voice dump) in the same power-on no longer reads a voice chip past the end of its flash, which silenced the voice until power-off.",
  "changes": {
    "fixes": [
      "A second full backup in the same power-on no longer silences the voices: chips on Tempester Voice are brought back to their start without reading past the end of their flash.",
      "A chip on DSI's Voice OS is read once per power-on; a second backup gets an empty message for it: power the machine off and on, then ask again.",
      "Send Voice OS over MIDI (Debug menu) follows the same rule: it sends nothing rather than a shifted image that could pass for a Voice OS."
    ]
  },
  "description": "1.6.7.0 with n°62 in its 1.6.8.0 form (patch/full_backup_1680.json in place of patch/full_backup.json), proved on the test build 1.6.8.0-a and on this image. Voice, Panel and SAM unchanged (Tempester Voice 1.5.1.1 is a Voice OS of its own, versions/voice/1.5.1.1.json). Installed on 14/11/2026 with Tempester Voice 1.5.1.1 on the six chips: two full backups in a row, identical byte for byte, the voices still playing.",
